==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|toucher}}, equivalent to {{af|en|touch|-er}}. The pejorative sense is derived from the sense of "[[touch]]ing" someone for money.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ʌtʃə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[touches]].
#* '''1853''', [[w:Charles Dickens|Charles Dickens]], ''Bleak House'', ch 4:
#*:We just twist up Chancery Lane, and cut along Holborn, and there we are in four minutes' time, as near as a '''toucher'''.
# {{lb|en|bowls}} A [[ball]] lying in contact with the [[jack]].
# {{lb|en|Geordie|pejorative}} A [[toucha]]; one who tries to get something out of others for nothing in return.

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=cehortu|Hectour|hectour|retouch}}

